I have created a new route at `app/timestamp/page.tsx` which forces dynamic rendering using `export const dynamic = 'force-dynamic'`. This ensures the timestamp is regenerated on every request, meeting the requirement to opt out of static prerendering without using cookies or headers.

```typescript
// app/timestamp/page.tsx

// Next.js: force dynamic rendering
export const dynamic = 'force-dynamic';

export default async function TimestampPage() {
  const timestamp = new Date().toISOString();

  return (
    <div className="flex min-h-screen flex-col items-center justify-center p-24">
      <h1 className="text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Server Timestamp</h1>
      <p className="text-xl font-mono bg-gray-100 p-4 rounded dark:bg-gray-800">
        {timestamp}
      </p>
      <p className="mt-4 text-sm text-gray-500">
        Refreshes on every request.
      </p>
    </div>
  );
}
```
